Switchboard, November 2026 (against megadiscord c915e03): bridge guild
channels one at a time. Upstream bridges a guild whole or not at all; the
login's metadata gains a per-channel choice, and the places that asked "is
this guild bridged?" ask about the channel instead. channelIsBridged also
checks the choice, so a deselected channel keeps its portal and room (and
their history) while its events are dropped. Resyncs and message fetches
read the choice when they run, not when they were queued, so work queued for
a channel does nothing once the channel is deselected. The helpers and the
provisioning endpoints are in overlay/pkg/connector/switchboard_channels.go.

